# {{lb|en|ambitransitive}} To [[retrain]] [[worker]]s in the [[skill]]s needed by [[modern]] [[business]], especially after [[redundancy]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Joseph Michalak; Stephen S. Pickering; Louis Uchitelle|quotee=Harris L. Sussman|title=Experts Divided On Jobs in the 90's|work=The New York Times|date=1989-04-16|url=https://www.nytimes.com/1989/04/16/jobs/experts-divided-on-jobs-in-the-90-s.html|issn=0362-4331|passage=In the existing work force also, not only among the new entrants, we are caught up in a treadmill of retraining, '''reskilling''', retooling the current work force for job descriptions that are as narrow and as shortsighted as the ones they have just come from.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|year=2018|month=January|work=World Economic Forum|title=Towards a Reskilling Revolution: A Future of Jobs|url=http://www3.weforum.org/docs/WEF_FOW_Reskilling_Revolution.pdf|passage=As the types of skills needed in the labour market change rapidly, individual workers will have to engage in life-long learning if they are to remain not just employable but are to achieve fulfilling and rewarding careers that allow them to maximize their employment opportunities. For companies, '''reskilling''' and upskilling strategies will be critical if they are to find the talent they need and to contribute to socially responsible approaches to the future of work.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Kevin Roose|title=The Hidden Automation Agenda of the Davos Elite|work=The New York Times|date=2019-01-25|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2019/01/25/technology/automation-davos-world-economic-forum.html|issn=0362-4331|passage=There are plenty of stories of successful '''reskilling''' — optimists often cite a program in Kentucky that trained a small group of former coal miners to become computer programmers — but there is little evidence that it works at scale.}}
# {{lb|en|ambitransitive}} To learn additional [[skill]]s.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2015|editors=Richard Eleftherios Boyatzis; Kylie Rochford; Scott N. Taylor|page=145|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=gS0qCwAAQBAJ&pg=PA145&dq=%22reskill%22&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwiWxeT14frKAhUS4WMKHYn4DEEQ6AEIJzAC#v=onepage&q=%22reskill%22&f=false|title=The Impact of Shared Vision on Leadership, Engagement, Organizational Citizenship and Coaching|passage=To maintain relevance and sustain marketable skills, IT professionals must '''reskill''' and '''reskill''' and '''reskill'''.}}

